rows.en:
Don't get mad, I'm not insulting you.
Hino said you're a cute kid he just can't leave alone.
No idea if that's true, though.{p}

Well, that was only at first.
My buddy's dead.
Now I can say flat out that that's how it is.{p}

...The movie tickets I'd bought for my buddy went to waste.
Thinking about that, one day after school I wandered over and looked into my buddy's old classroom.
It was pretty late, so the room was empty.{p}

She pressed her hands together toward the grave and stayed still for a while.
Her soft-looking hair slid smoothly over her shoulder.
For a second there, I thought I'd like to touch it.{p}

Still, when he called me from the hospital, he really sounded fine.
You never know what's coming, huh?
I pressed my hands together at my buddy's grave too.{p}

That was when she met my buddy, who'd been brought in after his traffic accident, and they hit it off.
He'd promised to take her to a movie after getting out of the hospital.
But my buddy was the one who died first...{p}

I see...
Yeah, that's what I thought, too.
I headed right back to school.{p}

...The next day, the doctor pronounced Lashes dead.
I heard they estimated the time of death from the state of her body.
She'd died right around the time I was running all over the school at night, looking for her.{p}

"Here, I'm giving you the ticket.
Don't let my buddy's feelings go to waste."
Then I pressed the ticket into the hand of Lashes' real body, lying on the bed.{p}

Clutched in her hand was the ticket, torn to tatters.
What was that scream I heard during class?
Was it what Lashes felt at the moment she died...?{p}

Hey, {a}.
Don't go putting this part in the article.
Got it?{p}
